{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Test-design / oracle matrix before production edits:\n- Persistence seam: one LIVE pass must write .tickets-tracker/.bridge_state/prev_snapshot.json as exactly {jira_key: {}}; a high-cardinality fixture must remain <=64 KiB. Existing cap-0/no-write tests remain the negative control.\n- Differ branch-2: >=900 prev-only full entries prove the raw differ emits unbound_local creates; the same key-set entries must emit zero creates.\n- Differ both-arm / production seam: {} prev entries may exercise raw field_drift, but run_differs must filter every field-bearing outbound snapshot-differ mutation before Jira; a genuinely curr-only key remains the positive inbound-create control.\n- Invariant seam: check_dual_identity_complete must return identical quarantine/repair outputs for realistic full snapshot entries versus {} entries.\n- Corpus artifact: replay >=4 consecutive real prev_snapshot revisions in both full->key-set and key-set->full directions and compare only Jira-reaching non-empty effects; print a machine-readable zero-difference result and snapshot byte sizes.\nOracle order: add tests/script first; demonstrate RED only at the persisted-shape seam; then make the smallest persistence change and rerun focused, related, lint, typecheck, and broader gates."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785718876736812001,"uuid":"8a2414d9-ed7f-4ded-b474-be1afa248e80"}